// Test: bugfixes/validator_fields_keep_later_values
// Grammar: function_call (validator.create, validator.field)
// Semantic: MEMORY_MODEL.md "Allocation" — compiled code allocates with the
//   module's `__malloc(size)`
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.182
// Expected output:
//   before alpha
//   beta
//   3
//
// Regression (#40): the validator functions called the host's
// `mem_alloc(type_id, size)` with the arguments swapped, so every block was
// as big as the type id (21 or 20 bytes, rounded to 24): the 640-byte field
// array of `validator.create()` got 24 bytes, and adding fields overwrote
// the list allocated after it (the run trapped in `names.get`). They now
// allocate with `__malloc(size)` like the rest of compiled code.

start:
	integer rules = validator.create()
	list<string> names = ["alpha", "beta", "gamma"]
	string label = "before " + names.get(0)
	// Changed in 0.33.184: validator.field/required follow stdlib-reference §15 (developer decision)
	validator.field(rules, "email", "ada@example.com")
	validator.required(rules)
	validator.field(rules, "age", "36")
	validator.minLength(rules, 3)
	print(label)
	print(names.get(1))
	print(names.size())
